Start with Default then Apply: 28 psi front / 23 psi rear, 30 L. Use smooth throttle and progressive lifts to adjust your line; carry momentum and allow time for the classic steering's longer travel. Build up in second and third before trying faster links. Begin with a slow roll at both steering locks and check wheel clearance and cockpit hands. The three exterior views show the left wheel, right wheel and rear action-camera position.
